## Google Drive backup & restore (Premium)

Drive is **manual backup/restore**, not live sync. Nothing uploads in the background.

### Where it lives in the app

**Settings → Data ownership → Backup your ArtCloset to Google Drive**

Requires active **VIP or Premium**, plus a Google OAuth client ID on the build. Free users see an unlock upsell only.

| Action | What happens |
|--------|----------------|
| **Connect Google** | Native Google account picker for Drive app-data access; account email shown in Settings |
| **Backup now** | Incremental: uploads the SQLite catalog plus only new or changed images to the user’s private Drive **app data folder** (not a normal My Drive folder). Each photo is stored once; the newest 3 snapshots are kept |
| **Restore from Drive** | Downloads the latest backup for that Google account and **replaces** the catalog on this device |
| **Disconnect** | Clears local Google tokens; the backup file stays in Google until overwritten by a later backup |

### Restore (user-facing rules)

1. Connect the **same Google account** that created the backup.
2. Tap **Restore from Drive** and confirm the warning.
3. Current local catalog is **overwritten** (no merge).
4. After restore, restart the app if Home or lists look stale.
5. If no backup exists for that account → *No Drive backup found*.
6. Expired Google session → Connect again, then restore.
7. Free or expired VIP → Drive restore stays locked; the local catalog still works.

### Where the file is in Google Drive

Backups use scope `drive.appdata`: one `artcloset-blob-*` file per photo, plus an `artcloset-catalog-*.db` and `artcloset-snapshot-*.json` per backup (1.0.3+). Restore still reads the older single `artcloset-backup.zip`, which is removed once 3 newer snapshots exist. Users typically **cannot** browse them in drive.google.com like a normal folder—recovery is through ArtCloset **Restore from Drive**.

### Setup note (builds)

OAuth client IDs (`GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID` / optional iOS) must be set in `.env` and EAS secrets; test Drive in a **dev, preview, or Play** build (not Expo Go). For Play installs, register Android OAuth SHA-1s for each signing cert, and if Connect fails with `DEVELOPER_ERROR` / code `10`, add the **Signer #1** SHA-1 from a Play-downloaded APK (`apksigner`). See [docs/VIP-AND-DRIVE.md](docs/VIP-AND-DRIVE.md) and [docs/PLAY-SHA1-GUIDE.md](docs/PLAY-SHA1-GUIDE.md).

